# Davian Martikov, master of the Wizard of Wines (docs/voice/davian_martikov.md). The Tarokka's Raven ally.
# start: the first meeting at the camp (approach), then his menu wherever he stands. The menu is where the party
# reports (winery cleared, stones, Yester Hill, Elvir); check_done gives the region's one milestone.
# When Davian travels as a guest, Stefania opens this menu instead (stefania:news).

~ start
if not flag.davian_met
-> first_meeting
endif
if flag.winery_strongbox_opened and not flag.davian_strongbox_noticed and flag.winery_reclaimed
-> strongbox
endif
if flag.winery_reclaimed
Davian: My house smells of druid. It will smell of wine again by spring or I'll know the reason. Speak.
else
Davian: Still alive. Good. Speak.
endif
-> menu

~ first_meeting
set davian_met
Narrator: An old man sits on an upturned cask by the fire with a blanket over his knees: white beard, black eyes, and the bearing of a king who has mislaid his kingdom and expects it returned by supper.
if flag.raven_harmed and not flag.adrian_apology_heard
Davian [angry]: You're the ones who struck my son out of the air on the Svalich road. Sit down. I can't afford to throw you out, and I hate that more than I hate you.
elif flag.keepers_of_the_feather_met
Davian: Urwin's friends. The birds have talked of nothing else for a week. Sit. You're shorter than they said.
elif flag.ilinca_vouched
Davian: Ilinca Vrana says you pulled two children out of a hag's oven. Ilinca doesn't say good things about anyone, so I expect it's true. Sit.
elif flag.wizard_of_wines_hook
Davian: Someone in Vallaki misses my wine, then. Good. So do I. Sit.
else
Davian: Strangers, at my fire. Either you've come to rob me, and you're three months late, or you've come to help, and you're very welcome. Sit.
endif
Davian: I am Davian Martikov. That was my winery up there until the druids of Yester Hill walked up my lane with the forest at their backs. Now my family lives under the trees like birds. Which, in fairness, we are.
interject guest:ireena: My father bought your wine for every feast day. He said it was the only honest thing that ever came up the road.
-> stones

~ stones
Davian: No vine should live in this valley; there's no sun worth the name. Ours do because three stones lie in their soil, green as new leaves, each the size of a plum. A wizard paid them to my family, long ago, for a winter's lodging.
Davian: One was stolen last autumn. The ravens followed the thief to Berez, the drowned village by the river, to the witch who lives there. One the druids carried off to their hill. The last I hid the night we fled.
Davian: They're tearing my house apart to find it. So far my house is winning.
if name:ratatoille and not (quest.a_seat_at_the_table >= a_winery)
-> companions/table:winery
endif
-> stones_menu

~ stones_menu
* [if not flag.winery_stone_hiding_told] Where did you hide it? -> hiding
* [if not flag.yester_hill_known] What do the druids want with a stone? -> druids_want
* [if not flag.davian_why_asked] Why did the druids come for you? -> why_us
* We'll clear your house. -> pledge

~ hiding
set winery_stone_hiding_told
Davian: Hm. You have honest faces, or faces that have practised. In the cellar, at the foot of the stair, stands the founder's cask, older than the house. It has a false end. Turn the third hoop and pull.
-> stones_menu

~ druids_want
set yester_hill_known
Davian: To starve us, first. A winery without wine is a farm with airs. And on Yester Hill, west of here, they're building a great figure of earth shaped like the lord in the castle. They mean to wake it with my stone for a heart.
Davian: My son Elvir went to watch that hill last spring. Don't ask me about it.
-> stones_menu

~ why_us
set davian_why_asked
Davian: Because a raven sees a great deal and repeats it in the right ears. My family has watched the lord in the castle for longer than he has known he was being watched. He knows now. This is his answer.
-> stones_menu

~ pledge
set davian_pledged
set winery_stone_hiding_told
set yester_hill_known
quest wizard_of_wines asked
quest the_third_stone told
if not flag.raven_harmed or flag.adrian_apology_heard
attitude davian_martikov friendly
endif
Davian: Then here are the terms. Drive them out of the winery and out of the press house. Bring up my stone from the founder's cask: cellar, foot of the stair, third hoop, pull. Then we'll talk about the hill.
Davian: I'll pay in the only coin I trust. Wine, when there's wine again. Until then, my gratitude, which is rarer.
if name:wren_featherfoot
interject name:wren_featherfoot: How many druids? Roughly. Asking for my knees.
else
interject tag:blunt: How many druids?
endif
Davian: Fewer than yesterday, if you start now.
-> menu

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- The menu

~ menu
* [if flag.winery_hall_cleared and flag.press_house_cleared and not flag.winery_reclaimed] The druids are out of your house. -> reclaim
* [if flag.winery_stone_recovered and not flag.winery_stone_returned] Your stone, from the founder's cask. -> return_cellar
* [if flag.yester_stone_recovered and not flag.yester_stone_returned] The stone from Yester Hill. -> return_hill
* [if flag.yester_hill_resolved and not flag.yester_hill_reported] Yester Hill is finished. -> hill_report
* [if quest.the_third_stone == found and not flag.berez_stone_returned] The witch's stone, from Berez. -> return_berez
* [if flag.elvir_remains_recovered and not flag.elvir_buried] We brought Elvir home. -> burial
* [if flag.elvir_truth_known and not flag.martikovs_reconciled] Elvir sent Adrian away. He wrote it on his cage. -> reconcile_proof
* [if flag.adrian_told_order and not flag.elvir_truth_known and not flag.martikovs_reconciled and not flag.davian_refused_once] Adrian says Elvir ordered him to fly. -> adrian_word
* [if flag.elvir_story_heard and not flag.martikovs_reconciled and not flag.davian_insight_tried] [Insight DC 14] It isn't Adrian you're angry with. -> insight_ok | insight_fail
* [if tarokka.ally.npc == davian_martikov and not guest:davian_martikov] Madam Eva's cards named you. -> ally
* [if not flag.winery_reclaimed] What's waiting for us in the winery? -> intel
* [name:hedda_ironvow] [if quest.cold_prayers and flag.keepers_of_the_feather_met and not flag.hedda_keepers_told] Ask about a silver raven with a sunburst in its claws. -> companions/prayers:davian
* [name:ratatoille] [if quest.a_seat_at_the_table and not (quest.a_seat_at_the_table >= a_winery)] Ask about the Wizard of Wines. -> companions/table:winery
* [name:ratatoille] [if flag.winery_reclaimed and not flag.ratatoille_supper_cooked] Ask for the use of the kitchen tonight. -> companions/table:supper
* Tell us about the winery. -> lore
* Goodbye. -> bye

~ intel
Davian: The druids sleep in the fermenting hall and feed my vats to their creatures. Their leader, a boy called Kostin, keeps to the press house with something he grew in my best vat. Some nights it sings to him.
if treasure_at:wizard_of_wines_press_house or treasure_at:wizard_of_wines_cellar
Davian: And one thing I can't account for. The ravens say a cold light shows in my house some nights, where no lamp is. If you find it, it isn't mine.
endif
-> menu

~ lore
Davian: My family pressed wine on this hill before the valley had its lord. The man on the sign is the wizard who paid us in stones. We set by a cask for him every year. He's never come for it. Wizards are poor at visiting.
if name:kip_smudgewick
interject name:kip_smudgewick: A creditor who never collects. Either very generous or very dead. I wish mine were either.
elif class:wizard and not name:ratatoille
interject class:wizard: A wizard who never collects a debt is either very generous or very dead.
else
interject tag:cynical: A man who never collects a debt is either very generous or very dead.
endif
Davian: I've drunk to both, in alternate years.
-> menu

~ bye
if flag.winery_reclaimed
Davian: Go carefully. Come back thirsty.
else
Davian: Go on. The house won't empty itself.
endif
-> END

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Reports

~ reclaim
set winery_reclaimed
quest wizard_of_wines reclaimed
Narrator: Davian lets the blanket fall and walks up the lane without a word. At the top he lays a hand flat on the winery door, the way you'd lay a hand on a horse that came home without its rider.
Davian: Hm. They've scratched the paint.
Davian: Stefania! Bring the children. We're going home.
if flag.kostin_doubts
Davian: The ravens saw the boy Kostin walk west, slowly, like a man who isn't sure where he's going anymore. Interesting.
elif flag.kostin_fled
Davian: The boy Kostin ran west, the ravens say, toward the hill. He'll warn them you're coming. Expect to be expected.
endif
-> check_done

~ return_cellar
set winery_stone_returned
set winery_stones_returned += 1
Narrator: Davian takes the stone in both hands. Green light comes up between his fingers, the way sun comes through a leaf.
Davian: Hello, old friend. You hid well. Better than I did.
Narrator: He carries it to the nearest row and presses it into the soil with his thumb. For a moment nothing happens. Then the vine above it makes a small sound, like a cork easing out of a bottle.
-> first_wine

~ return_hill
set yester_stone_returned
set winery_stones_returned += 1
if flag.gulthias_tree_burned
Narrator: The second stone is warm and smells faintly of smoke. Davian turns it over twice, looking for the tree in it, and doesn't find any.
else
Narrator: The second stone has a dark thread through it now, fine as a hair. Davian holds it up to the light for a long moment.
Davian: It's been near that tree. Good soil will draw it out, in time. Most things wash out, in time.
endif
Davian: Two. Two in the ground. My grandfather had only two for a while, when he was a boy, and he swore the wine was better for having to try.
-> first_wine

~ return_berez
set berez_stone_returned
set winery_stones_returned += 1
quest the_third_stone returned
Narrator: Davian doesn't take the third stone at once. He looks at it in your hand, then at you, and his face does something it hasn't done since you met him.
Davian: From the witch. From Berez. You went into that drowned place for my vines. ...Three. I didn't think I'd see three again before I died. I find I'm in less of a hurry now.
-> first_wine

~ first_wine
if flag.winery_reclaimed and flag.winery_stones_returned >= 1 and not flag.winery_wine_flows
set winery_wine_flows
Davian: Then the press runs again. Not this week; the grapes need a month to remember themselves. But the cellar still holds what we pressed before they came, and the cart in the yard has three good wheels.
Davian: The first cart goes where you say. You've earned that much.
* To Vallaki. Urwin's inn has been pouring the last cask for weeks. -> cart_vallaki
* To the village under the castle. They have less than anyone. -> cart_village
* To Krezk. A town behind walls that high needs something to keep its spirits up. -> cart_krezk
endif
-> check_done

~ cart_vallaki
set winery_first_cart = "vallaki"
Davian: To Urwin, then. He'll pretend he isn't pleased. He gets that from me.
-> check_done

~ cart_village
set winery_first_cart = "village"
Davian: To the village. The shopkeeper there will try to charge them double for it. The ravens will see that he doesn't.
-> check_done

~ cart_krezk
set winery_first_cart = "krezk"
Davian: To Krezk. They keep their gate shut to strangers and open it for my carts. If you're going that way, walk beside the casks. A gate that opens for wine might open for you.
-> check_done

~ hill_report
set yester_hill_reported
if guest:adrian_martikov
leave adrian_martikov
Narrator: Adrian walks into the yard ahead of you and stops in front of his father. Neither of them says a word. Then Davian takes his son by the shoulder, once, hard, and lets go.
elif flag.adrian_went_to_hill
Davian: You took my son up that hill and brought him back down it. I'll not forget that.
endif
if flag.gulthias_tree_burned
Davian: The ravens saw the smoke from here: one black column, straight up, as if the hill were being emptied. Good. Let it burn to the roots.
else
Davian: The figure broken and the druids scattered. And the tree? Still standing, the ravens say. Hm. Trees are patient. So are ravens.
endif
if flag.yester_druids_fate == "killed"
Davian: And Ruxandra is dead. I knew her when she was a girl who picked my grapes for a copper a basket. I'll drink to who she was. Not to what she became.
elif flag.yester_druids_fate == "spared" or flag.yester_druids_fate == "fled"
Davian: And Ruxandra lives, somewhere out there. Mercy's a fine thing. Remember that you chose it, if she comes back.
endif
if not flag.winery_reclaimed
quest wizard_of_wines hill_broken
Davian: Now come and do the same to the ones sleeping in my house.
endif
-> check_done

~ check_done
if flag.winery_reclaimed and flag.yester_hill_resolved and not flag.wizard_of_wines_milestone_reached
-> milestone
endif
if flag.winery_reclaimed and flag.winery_stones_returned >= 2 and not flag.keepers_allied
-> keepers_oath
endif
-> menu

~ milestone
set wizard_of_wines_milestone_reached
quest wizard_of_wines saved
xp milestone
Narrator: That night the Martikovs broach a cask from before the druids came, and the whole family drinks in the yard under a sky with no stars in it, and for an hour nobody looks up.
Davian: To the hill, broken. To the house, ours. And to strangers, who it turns out are good for something.
if name:godrick_pendlebrook
interject name:godrick_pendlebrook: Good for something! That's the nicest thing anyone's said about me in this whole valley.
else
interject tag:cheerful: That's the nicest thing anyone's said about me in this whole valley.
endif
if name:liriel_dawnsong
interject name:liriel_dawnsong: The dawn comes slower to some places than others. It comes. Morning's grace on this house.
else
interject tag:pious: Good wine. Dawn comes slower to some places than others. It comes.
endif
-> check_done

~ keepers_oath
set keepers_allied
Narrator: Davian whistles two notes. Ravens come down out of the trees, off the eaves, off the roof of the press house, until the yard is black with them and every one is looking at you.
Davian: The Keepers of the Feather owe you two stones and a house, and ravens don't forget a debt. Wherever you go in this valley, look up. If you need word carried or eyes on a place, say so out loud.
if flag.raven_harmed
Davian: Even you. My son says you're not as bad as your aim. Ravens have long memories, but we're not unreasonable.
endif
-> menu

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Elvir

~ burial
set elvir_buried
Narrator: They bury Elvir at the end of the last green row, under the cairn they raised for him when there was nothing to put beneath it. Stefania sings. Davian doesn't. Adrian digs, and won't let anyone else hold the spade.
Davian: He's home. That's the thing. Whatever else is true, he's home.
if flag.elvir_truth_known and not flag.martikovs_reconciled
Narrator: At the graveside Davian keeps looking at Adrian, like a man who has something to say and has forgotten the language it's in.
endif
-> check_done

~ reconcile_proof
Narrator: You tell him what was scratched into the post of the last cage. Davian listens without moving, the way old men listen to weather coming.
Davian: "I sent him." ...Elvir. You stubborn, stupid boy. You always did think you were the eldest.
-> reconcile

~ adrian_word
Davian: Then why didn't he say so? He's had a year. A year of me looking through him at supper.
* [Persuasion DC 14] Because he knew you'd call it an excuse. Are you going to prove him right? -> adrian_word_ok | adrian_word_fail
* We don't know. -> adrian_word_drop

~ adrian_word_ok
Narrator: Davian opens his mouth to answer, and doesn't. He looks across to where Adrian is scrubbing a cask he has already scrubbed twice.
-> reconcile

~ adrian_word_fail
set davian_refused_once
Davian [angry]: Don't tell me what my son meant. I know what my son meant. I knew him before you knew this valley had a name.
-> menu

~ adrian_word_drop
set davian_refused_once
Davian: No. You don't. Neither do I.
-> menu

~ insight_ok
set davian_insight_tried
Narrator: He holds his hands like a man holding something that isn't there anymore. It isn't his son he can't forgive. He sent two boys to watch that hill, and one came back.
Davian: ...I sent them. I sent them to that hill. And I couldn't look at the one who came home, because then I'd have to look at the one who sent them.
-> reconcile

~ insight_fail
set davian_insight_tried
Narrator: His face is a shut door with good locks. Whatever is behind it, you won't have it today, and perhaps neither will he.
-> menu

~ reconcile
set martikovs_reconciled
quest elvir_martikov reconciled
Narrator: He gets up. He's an old man, and it takes a while. He goes to where his son is working, and they stand there, two men with the same black eyes, and neither of them is any good at this.
Davian: Adrian. The press is yours. My knees are finished with it.
Adrian: Your knees are fine.
Davian: Then take it anyway.
if name:thistle
interject name:thistle: Good. That's good.
else
interject tag:loyal: Good. That's good.
endif
interject guest:ireena: My father and my brother never said it either. Not once, before the end. I'm glad somebody did.
-> check_done

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- The strongbox in the office

~ strongbox
set davian_strongbox_noticed
Davian: Someone has been in my strongbox. It was a good lock. It was a good lock for forty years.
* [if gold >= 60] We took what was in it. Here it is, all of it. -> strongbox_return
* We opened it to see if the druids had. We took nothing. -> strongbox_claim
* Call it our fee. -> strongbox_fee
* [Deception DC 14] The druids, surely. -> strongbox_lie | strongbox_lie_caught

~ strongbox_return
gold -60
attitude davian_martikov friendly
Davian: Hm. A thief who brings it back is either a fool or an honest man having a bad week. I'll assume the second. Keep ten for the lock.
gold +10
-> menu

~ strongbox_claim
Davian: Then we'll find out when I count it, won't we. I'll count it later, alone, like a miser. It's a family tradition.
-> menu

~ strongbox_fee
set winery_strongbox_kept
Davian: Your fee. My father paid men to clear wolves from these rows, and they charged less, and they were also thieves. Fine. It's paid.
-> menu

~ strongbox_lie
Davian: The druids. Of course. Filthy creatures, druids. No respect for a good lock.
Narrator: He frowns at the lock for a long while afterwards, and then lets it be.
-> menu

~ strongbox_lie_caught
set winery_strongbox_kept
Davian: Druids don't pick locks. They don't need to; they grow through them. Don't lie to me in my own house. You're not good enough at it yet.
-> menu

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- The Tarokka's Raven

~ ally
if not flag.winery_reclaimed
set davian_ally_asked
Davian: A Vistani crone shuffled her deck and my name fell out. Hm. I'll go where her cards say, and gladly, once there are no druids asleep in my bed. Not before. A man doesn't leave his house to squatters.
-> menu
endif
if flag.davian_ally_asked
Davian: You asked before. My house is mine again. Ask me now.
endif
Davian: Eva. Of course it was Eva. She bought wine from my father and haggled him to tears. If her cards say the old raven flies with you, then the old raven flies with you.
if flag.martikovs_reconciled
Davian: Adrian has the press. Stefania has the house. I have nothing left to do here but get in the way. Better I get in his way.
else
Davian: Stefania will mind the house. Adrian will mind the vines. He's good at being left behind.
endif
if flag.winery_strongbox_kept
Davian: I'll be counting the spoons, mind.
endif
join davian_martikov
quest find_the_ally found
interject class:wizard: Will you fly with us, or above us?
Davian: Whichever annoys the enemy more.
-> END
